| D-011 | 2026-10-27 | all orgs     | CI provider is GitHub Actions (default), CircleCI, or both, chosen with hull pieces `circleci`/`circleci-only`; required check names never change (CircleCI's ci-ok is mirrored to a commit status); governance, PR previews, splice bot and releases stay on GitHub Actions; D-007 rules apply to CircleCI. [why](decisions/011-ci-providers.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-014 | 2026-11-03 | all          | Approval policy after bootstrap mode is the intake answer `[approvals] policy` in `.bosun/intake.toml`: `owner` (default when unset), `owner-gated` (orchestrator approves low-risk and R-ci after green checks and an independent review; owner approves R-gov, `.bosun`, approval code, workflows, secrets, releases) or `orchestrator`. In every policy the owner approves environment deployments, decisions merges, branch rules and secrets, and CI-workflow or composite-action PRs are owner-class. Repos are created and configured only by the org provisioner app via keelstackhq/provision, gated by a one-hour, single-use orchestrator signature made on an owner form answer; secrets are environment-only; no PAT. [why](decisions/014-zero-touch-onboarding.md) |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-016 | 2026-11-05 | all          | No line cap: bosun plans each epic as one PR (coupled, or testable only whole) or a parallel split (independent tasks); gated paths (workflows, templates, contract, governance, .bosun, approval/risk code, secrets, releases, risk:high) stay at most 400 lines, one task, alone; big PRs get chunked review listing every chunk; >2x planned size is a re-plan note, never a block. [why](decisions/016-pr-shape-follows-the-goal.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-017 | 2026-11-05 | all          | Autonomous mode: the orchestrator approves (signs bosun approvals) and merges every PR itself, gated and decisions PRs included, after green CI and an independent review verdict on the exact head; no owner forms. Gate-weakening PRs (R-weaken), GitHub human-only steps (environment taps) and secrets stay with the owner; agents never force-push; ends when the owner says so. [why](decisions/017-autonomous-mode.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-018 | 2026-11-10 | all          | Every owner approval is asked in chat (AskUserQuestion; Claude Tag thread reply); the owner's yes is the approval, recorded only by an orchestrator session via `bosun approve <pr>@<head> --chat` naming the exact head SHA; it counts under every policy, R-weaken included, and goes stale on a new push; signing keys optional; child sessions hand questions to the orchestrator. Bootstrap mode from D-012 stays until 2026-11-30 UTC. [why](decisions/018-chat-approvals.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-019 | 2026-11-10 | all          | D-015 merge and release rules stay (children never merge, tag, release or force-push; orchestrator merges on green required checks plus any owner approval; releases via the release workflow, owner taps `release`; decisions owner-merged). Repos with `[ci] provider = "none"` merge only via orchestrator-only `bosun merge <pr>`, which re-checks gate stamps, risk, review verdict and approval on the head locally; every other agent merge path stays refused. [why](decisions/019-merges-with-and-without-ci.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
